>>
Rule 1 (input must be a tensor object, not a dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (min/max are well-defined for non-empty inputs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) then true else min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (all dimensions must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (scalar inputs are allowed; otherwise the leading dimension is valid)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 0
